How is a culture formed?
There are many types of cultures and they form in different ways. First of all, i believe that the lifestyle and expressions of people in a specific area over a long time can be considered a culture. This kind of culture is shaped by factors like climate, geography, and traditions passed down through generations. Additionally, in modern society, various organizations whether they're companies, school or sports teams, develop their own unique cultures. These cultures are based on shared values and goals among the people involved. They believe that having a strong culture can help everyone work together.

What kinds of videos are popular in your country?
Firstly, comedy videos are extremely popular. In today's fast-paced society. Life can be quite stressful and many people turn to short videos for entertainment. Watching funny clips allows they to unwind and escape from their daily presures, making it a go-to choice for quick laugh. Additionally, educational videos haved gained significant traction. With the rise of online learning, acquiring knowledge has become more accessible than ever. More and more people are looking to use their free time to improve their skills and prepare for future opportunities.

Why are so many young people obsessed with short videos?
Firstly, short video platforms cover a wide range of content, providing users with abundant viewing choice. We can choose to watch anything we are interested in wherther it's vlogs, commentary, or even learning a skill. With a constant flow of new videos available every day in every category, it's easy to get hooked. Secondly, there platforms offer personalized recommendations base on user interests. As we scroll through short videos, the algorithms recognize our preferences and continuously push content we enjoy. This creates a cycle where viewers find it hard to put their phones down.

How can a person be a good co-worker?
To be a good workmate, a person should definitely have a few essential qualities. First, it's important to find common ground while respecting differences. While having a shared goal is curcial, each person brings their own unique ideas to the table. Valuing these diverse perspectives fosters a more collaborative environment. Second, embracing a collaborative spirit is key. Collaboration isn't about competing with each other, it's about working together to achieve goals. If someone is jealous of a colleague's ideas or successes, it can create friction and hinder process.

How important is it to have a variety of payment options?
It is extremely important and necessary. First of all, it is more occommodating for people of all age groups. In my country, electronic payments like scanning QR codes have become very popular and many shop no longer accept cash. This can post a challenge for older adults who are unfimilar with digital payment methods. Moreover, having diverse payment options can be curcial in emergency situations. For instance, if your phone dies and you won't be able to use mobile payments and even renting a power bank can become difficult. In such cases, having the ability to pay with cash or a credit card can really save the day.

Should the media only publish good news?
Definitely not. First of all, it's the media's responsibility to inform the public. People have the right to know what's happening in the world including both positive and negative news, right? If the video only shares good news,it creates an incomplete picture and prevents us from understanding the complexity of societal issues. Moreover, reporting on negative events can serve a crucial purpose. For instance, many legal affairs programs reveal the darker sides of the society and show the consequences of crime. This kind of reporting can deter potential offenders.

